One option for the "opt in" model of `TypeConverters` is to respect the `TypeConverterAttribute` if either:

* Directly applied to the property
* Directly applied to the Type of the property

So, for example:

```C#
[TypeConverter(typeof(PointConverter))]
public struct Point
{
   public int X;
   public int Y;
}

public class CustomOptions
{
    public Point CurrentPoint { get; set }
}
```

or

```C#
public struct Point
{
   public int X;
   public int Y;
}

public class CustomOptions
{
    [TypeConverter(typeof(PointConverter))]
    public Point CurrentPoint { get; set }
}
```
See also:

* https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/issues/44493#issuecomment-1425503530
* https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/issues/36545
